  "reconstructionNotes": "Two-zone layout. Top third: three small stages side by side labeled (a), (b), (c) — (a) is the bare term T(n) at far left, (b) is a two-node-deep tree with root cn, (c) is three levels deep with four T(n/4) leaves. Bottom two-thirds: stage (d), a centered binary tree drawn with thin straight black edges, root cn at top center, cn/2 pair, cn/4 quartet, then short dashed stubs, then vertical dotted lines down to a bottom row of c leaves with a • • • ellipsis in the middle. A wide curly brace under the leaf row is labeled n. A tall double-headed arrow on the far left spans the tree, labeled lg n. On the right, a dotted horizontal arrow leaves each drawn level and lands in a vertical column where every entry reads cn, with a ⋮ between the third and last entries; a short horizontal rule sits below the column above 'Total: cn lg n + cn'. All text in serif italic math style, black on white. Use color only as interaction feedback: unresolved T(·) nodes in a muted gray/dashed outline, resolved cost nodes in solid black, the active level highlighted in a single accent color (e.g. amber) with its row sum badge '2^i × cn/2^i = cn' appearing beside it when the overlay is on. Node spacing should compress gracefully as n grows so wider leaf rows still fit the frame."
}

The second image above is a screenshot of the PREVIOUS attempt's rendered output (not the source figure) — use it to see exactly what broke.

Here is the generated code to evaluate:

<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<p id="demoNarration" style="margin:0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#222"></p>
<span style="display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center">
  <button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button>
